You have to buy me some time, though

269
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,180
You're really putting me on the spot here

270
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:52,020
How am I supposed to distract them?

271
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:52,840
You could say

272
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,600
Nice weather we're having, huh?

273
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:55,520
Just like that

274
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,260
Nice weather we're having, huh?

275
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,020
Remember

276
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,400
Don't take your eyes off what's-her-face

277
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,080
If you can do that, we'll be good

278
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:02,720
Okay, fine!

279
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:10,480
I'll clear a pathway for you

280
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,540
Don't worry, Stinky

281
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:12,360
Just fly

282
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,240
Oh, right

283
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,520
Thanks for the backup

284
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:17,140
And would you please stop calling me Stinky?

285
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,660
Stop right there!

286
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:20,160
Huh?

287
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:22,900
Judging from those wings, you must be a goddess

288
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:27,360
If you're on gear branday, that means you have that meathead hero with you

289
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:30,640
Yeah, well, he wanted me to relay a message

290
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,940
Let her go!

291
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:33,360
Not to worry

292
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:36,700
I was just using this girl as bait to lure the hero out

293
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:38,780
Wait, you're seriously gonna release her?

294
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,980
Yes, but only once I'm considerably higher

295
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:46,080
In honor of your hero's downfall, I'm preparing a reverse firework

296
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:49,160
Any thoughts?

297
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:52,780
Is this not an excellent hype for you to make a beautiful firework?

298
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:01,100
I'm gonna make you apologize for the men you killed if it's the last thing I do!

299
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:07,260
Considering you're about to join those men, I'd say you're in no position to demand apologies

300
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:08,600
You bastard!

301
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,420
That's enough!

302
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,220
Your hero said he would be back by now

303
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,360
Is he still training?

304
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:14,060
Not in front of the bug!

305
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:14,780
Huh?

306
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:15,620
Training?

307
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:18,600
That means he's planning to attack me with a bow and arrow

308
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:21,180
Oh, well, that's just great!

309
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,480
He's a psychic too!

310
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:25,660
Guess I'll have to gain more altitude to really set this one off!

311
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:36,880
He's flying higher, so magic arrows have no chance of hitting him!

312
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,540
Way to be the worst distraction ever, Rista!

313
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:42,920
He he he!

314
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:47,300
Now to treat myself to the sight of you exploding into tiny red and pink pieces!

315
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:52,140
Hmm, I'll have to fling you to the ground as hard as I can so she can't catch you!

316
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:54,940
If he throws her with all his strength, I'll never catch her!

317
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:56,960
Hey, coward!

318
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:59,640
Get back on the ground and fight me like a man!

319
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:02,260
I'm not a man, I just dress like one!

320
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,340
The only thing you'll be fighting is gravity!

321
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:06,500
Ah, I'm out of options!

322
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:08,200
Ah!

323
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:09,560
Huh?

324
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:12,260
So, nice weather we're having, huh?

325
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:15,160
Life above the clouds, am I right?

326
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,620
Um, what are you talking about?

327
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,740
Uh, I have no idea!

328
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:21,520
Anytime now, Seiya!

329
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:27,660
Ah!

330
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:29,820
Gotcha!

331
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:33,560
Whoa, didn't factor in the weight of your armor!

332
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:35,440
It's pretty heavy, but I think we're gonna be okay!

333
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:36,740
Sorry about that.

334
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,340
That was Shining Arrow.

335
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:41,740
Somehow Seiya managed to reach him, but...

336
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:43,020
Doesn't make any sense!

337
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,460
Even magic arrows don't have that range!

338
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:48,000
I've done my research, and it's not possible!

339
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:49,860
Oh yeah? Why is that?

340
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:53,400
I factored in the effective trajectory when I flew this high up!

341
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:57,680
I don't care what magic arrows he's using, there's no way they could span such distance!

342
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,300
My hero is one in a hundred million, bub!

343
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:01,560
Get used to disappointment!

344
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:04,660
However gifted he is, it's still unlikely.

345
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:08,880
He doubtlessly flew after us until he was close enough to fire off a shot!

346
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:13,840
Like a stalker outside a window, he's hiding somewhere in the clouds as we speak.

347
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:18,580
His brain may be fly-sized, but he's just as perceptive as Seiya.

348
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:22,040
I am the fastest of all the Demon Lord's forces in the air!

349
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:24,640
You may call me the Lord of the Skies!

350
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:28,100
I have no clue where you are, Seiya, but you better not miss him again!

351
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:31,620
Oh, hero! I would exceedingly like to see your bow skills!

352
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,380
I won't even hide from you!

353
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:40,060
Scale of one to ten, how confident are you in your stupid hero right now?

354
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:41,680
Um, I'd say a ten?

355
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,640
I mean, he said that cheesy line...

356
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:51,980
Seven lights? Is that a seven-shot shining arrow?

357
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:54,760
He's trying to one-up the goddess of freaking archery!

358
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:56,760
It can't be avoided!

359
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:03,180
He he he he! Rolling dodge!

360
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,480
He evaded all seven!

361
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,900
No! Is this when we lose Seiya?

362
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:12,440
Kei and Brandi is basically the ultimate difficulty level!

363
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:13,520
There you are!

364
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,540
I'm coming, hero!

365
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:18,880
Seiya, watch out! You're no match for him in the air!

366
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:21,700
He he he he!

367
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:29,380
That hurts!

368
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:30,480
Holy...

369
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:31,480
Oh...

370
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,180
This bites!

371
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:34,180
Huh?

372
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:37,500
Are those magic lights or magic birds?

373
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:40,460
That kind of technique definitely belongs to Seiya!

374
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:41,980
But when did he use it?

375
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:42,960
I get it.

376
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:47,540
Once Beelbub dodged the arrows, they became birds and flew back like a boomerang!

377
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,600
I think you're right!

378
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:52,360
I bet it has a ridiculous name like Transform Automatic Garuda!

379
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:53,640
That's why Seiya!

380
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:54,920
Damn you!

381
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:57,940
I'm gonna be the firework now!

382
00:16:58,640 --> 00:16:59,020
Ah!

383
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:03,020
What goes on in that beautiful head of his?

384
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:07,820
Even though he outdid Meet Us by two arrows, he made a backup attack just in case they missed!

385
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:14,640
Seiya Ryukyuan, the only guy tough enough to save Gei Brandi, while staying cautious every step of the way!

386
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,840
And looking damn fine doing it!

387
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:21,140
Thank goodness you're safe, Captain Rosalie.

388
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:22,280
Yeah.

389
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:24,280
Master!

390
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:27,140
That was fan-freaking-tastic!

391
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:30,460
It really was! That bug brain didn't stand a chance!

392
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:34,560
Hey, hotshot! Pretty slick move! The Transform Automatic Garuda!

393
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:36,280
What are you babbling about now?

394
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:37,200
Oh, sorry!

395
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:39,180
That's just a silly name I came up with.

396
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:43,720
So what's it called? You know, that move when your light arrows turn into birds and ricochet back!

397
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:46,360
Oh, you're referring to Boomerang Birdie Boom Boom.

398
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:49,440
What? That's awful! You can't seriously call it that!

399
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,700
I didn't think of it until just this second.

400
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:54,760
Ugh! Gray, feel free to use my name if you want.

401
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,600
I don't want to. It's way too long and stinks as bad as you do.

402
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:00,060
You're so mean! Nothing about me stinks!

403
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:06,000
The title of hero doesn't suit you. Your victory was anything but chivalrous.

404
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:11,940
A true hero is someone who strikes down his foe without trickery. Just like my father does.

405
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:16,460
Now look! Rosalie, the only reason you're standing here right now is because of Seiya!

406
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:20,740
You could at least thank him! A little help here? Just try not to be offensive.

407
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,280
Nothing I say will make a difference, so let's drop it.

408
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:25,560
Barky just likes the sound of her own words.

409
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,200
What was that?

410
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:29,660
She's losing it again!

411
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:35,020
Whether it's shooting arrows or slinging insects, Seiya's lethal in everything he does.

412
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:47,100
Okay. Time to take out the remaining flies.

413
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:50,420
Tater Tot, short stack. Let's see what you're made of.

414
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:55,180
Really? They're letting the kids take the reins? That's so sweet of you!

415
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:56,560
It's not like I'm blind or anything.

416
00:18:57,340 --> 00:19:00,900
I can tell they've been training and have not only leveled up, but also gained abilities.

417
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:02,900
No! We have!

418
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:03,820
It's true!

419
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:06,720
Pop to it. I want to see maximum effort out there.

420
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,180
I'll make you proud! Wait and see!

421
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,360
Yeah! Wait and see!

422
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:09,420
Wait and see!

423
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:10,760
Nice.

424
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:10,880
Faster!

425
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:13,380
I feel betrayed. So very betrayed.

426
00:19:13,380 --> 00:19:16,880
You're up, short stack. Speed Tater's up with your haste magic.

427
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:19,340
Oh, sure.

428
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:23,460
Perfect. Now use dragon hands to collect fly corpses.

429
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,040
Okay, cool.

430
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,040
Nice.

431
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,040
Nice.

432
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,040
This method is much more efficient. It's also really entertaining me.

433
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:31,420
I feel betrayed. I feel betrayed. So very betrayed.

434
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,420
You're up, short stack. Speed Tater's up with your haste magic.

435
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:35,800
Oh, sure.

436
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:41,380
Perfect. Now use dragon hands to collect fly corpses.

437
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,120
Okay, cool.

438
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:53,240
Nice. This method is much more efficient. It's also really entertaining me.

439
00:19:58,620 --> 00:20:00,460
Good enough. I'll take it from here.

440
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:02,780
Cast Hell's Fire!

441
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:09,060
Am I a dragon or a maid?

442
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:13,780
I don't even know what to say to them in this situation.

443
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:18,800
Eliminating the stragglers? Isn't that beneath you, hero?

444
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:22,760
I'm not the biggest fan of your attitude, so you can take it with you when you leave!

445
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:26,380
Captain Rosalie, we need to tell them about the you-know-what before we go.

446
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:27,700
I was getting to that, okay?

447
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:28,300
God!

448
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:31,460
We may not see eye to eye, but there's something you should know.

449
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:32,340
Hmm?

450
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:36,180
Listen up. In a shrine near the village of Isale, there is a suit of armor.

451
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:39,360
This legendary armor will help you defeat the demon lord.

452
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,820
I'm sorry, it's legendary?

453
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:43,080
Not just legendary. Ultimate.

454
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:46,480
It was crafted by an ancient sage who foresaw our current crisis.

455
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:51,080
Our plan was to inform the hero as soon as he appeared, but the fly sidetracked us.

456
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:55,460
The knights of Rosegard have kept watch over the years, justly protecting the sacred treasure.

457
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:58,380
You all must be grateful, and I really can't blame you.

458
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,940
Sounds sketchy. Real sketchy.

459
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,880
Are you positive it's not cursed armor?

460
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:07,300
How could anyone curse it if it was always being watched? It wouldn't be sacred anymore!

461
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:11,260
Never know. The armor could be cursed, sacred, and legendary at the same time.

462
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,360
Yes, there is!

463
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,280
How can someone as irritating as you be dubbed a hero?

464
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:19,920
That armor should be worn by a gallant and noble man who's proven himself like my father.

465
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:22,700
YAH!

466
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:25,160
Oh! Please excuse us, Mr. Hero!

467
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:37,940
Before anything else, I say we go to that village and snag this armor.

468
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,440
And maybe get some rest while we're at it.

469
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:43,180
I could use a break from naked goddesses and fly monsters.

470
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:45,980
Yeah, a nap sounds pretty good to me.

471
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:46,700
Whatevs.

472
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:49,040
I use some MP for my magic bow.

473
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,160
I say we stop at the end so we can recharge.

474
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,060
Oh, Joy!

475
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:56,220
No, but we were just here.

476
00:22:01,780 --> 00:22:03,800
They leveled an entire village.

477
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:05,880
Hey, look! Over there!

478
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,940
That's the item shop!

479
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:11,320
We have to help!

480
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:20,500
Well, well, we meet again, hero.

481
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:24,300
You can sheathe your sword since I'm the one who summoned this creature.

482
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:24,840
Huh?

483
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:27,500
It's an Adamantois.

484
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:31,860
A gargantuan demon I brought forth from a whole other world.

485
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:34,900
Hey, P-Pants.

486
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:37,860
If you're going to call me a name, I prefer you use...

487
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:40,120
Summon or kill Kapoor.

488
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:41,720
One of the four heavenly kings.

489
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:44,360
We've got supplies from one of the four heavenly kings?

490
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:49,960
Thanks to my crystal ball, I've been observing you and your motley crew bearing witness to your adventures.

491
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:54,320
You've had your fun, but I think you've meddled in Gaya Brande long enough.

492
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,860
That humongous turtle! That's why you summoned it!

493
00:22:57,140 --> 00:22:58,300
You're trying to take out Ziya!

494
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:01,360
You assume much, though you were right in one regard.

495
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:03,640
Adamantois is here for a reason.

496
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:07,260
And that's the reason?

497
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:12,080
Yes. The sacred armor is now nothing more than a pile of scraps.

498
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:16,460
It was made from adamantite, the strongest metal in Gaya Brande.

499
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:19,140
Ordinarily, no one would be able to break it.

500
00:23:19,740 --> 00:23:21,500
No! Come on!

501
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:26,080
I destroyed the armor before you could get your filthy human hands on it.

502
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:29,840
Just our luck. We're all for two in the legendary equipment department.

503
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:30,580
Hero.

504
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:35,380
Unlike most mortals, you had a slim chance of defeating the demon lord.

505
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:39,300
But I guess we'll never know for certain since your journey ends here.

